// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// TIER INTEGRITY — the declared above-tier residency exceptions (sc-15799)
//
// THE INVARIANT (normative statement: `docs/memory-strategy-contract.md`, "Tier integrity"):
//
//     No component is resident above the user's selected quant tier unless a DECLARED, MEASURED
//     exception says otherwise.
//
// Choosing q8 or q4 *is* a memory decision. If a user picks q4 because bf16 does not fit, carrying any
// component at bf16 defeats the choice they made. This file is the catalog's complete answer to "which
// components sit above the selected tier, on which tiers, and at what cost" — the audit sc-15799
// demanded. `scripts/check-tier-integrity.mjs` validates it, generates `docs/generated/tier-integrity.md`
// from it, and fails the `parity` lane on drift.
//
// WHAT THE AUDIT FOUND, stated plainly: above-tier residency is NOT rare. On a q4 or q8 tier the great
// majority of image entries keep a VAE, a text encoder, or both resident at bf16 or f32. The story that
// opened this expected a handful; the honest count is most of the catalog. That is why this file exists
// as a ledger rather than a footnote — and why every row carries an in-tree citation for the FACT even
// where the COST is not yet measured.
//
// ROW SHAPE
//   model            catalog entry id in config/manifests/builtin.models.jsonc
//   component        which component is above tier (textEncoder / vae / visionTower / controlBranch /
//                    identityAdapters / transformerHead)
//   residentTier     the precision it is actually resident at: "bf16" | "f32" | "q8"
//   appliesToTiers   the SELECTED tiers on which it is above tier (never includes a tier at or below
//                    residentTier — the checker enforces this)
//   backends         which lanes carry it: ["mlx"], ["candle"], or both. Omit for both.
//   cause            "packing-exception"   a deliberate quality decision: this component is not packed
//                                          because packing it measurably or structurally hurts.
//                    "backend-capability"  the backend cannot serve the on-disk format, so it upcasts.
//                                          Packing cannot fix this; a compute path or a re-host can.
//                    "structural"          there is nothing quantizable (all-conv, folded-away leaves).
//   reason           one sentence, in the terms the provider itself uses.
//   evidence.state   "measured"   `costGb` (or costBytes) is a real in-tree number, with a source
//                    "unmeasured" no isolated component cost exists in the tree yet; `owedBy` names the
//                                 story that owes it. LEGAL ONLY for the entries grandfathered by
//                                 sc-15799 (enumerated in the checker) — a NEW entry cannot ship one.
//   evidence.source  file:line where the fact (and the number, when measured) is recorded in-tree.
//   evidence.owedBy  the story that owes the measurement, when unmeasured.
//
// A NOTE ON HONESTY. Most `unmeasured` rows are unmeasured because the tree records the component's
// precision but never its isolated size — the manifest carries per-tier TOTALS. Estimating a component
// split from a total would be inventing evidence, so these say "unmeasured" and name sc-16015. The
// checker's ratchet means that list can only shrink.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
{
  "$schema": "../packages/schemas/tier-integrity.schema.json",
  // Entries GRANDFATHERED with an unmeasured cost by sc-15799. The checker rejects an `unmeasured` row
  // for any model not on this list, so a new model cannot ship an unmeasured exception; and the list may
  // only ever shrink (sc-16015 empties it). It lives in the checker, not here, so that editing this file
  // cannot widen the amnesty.
  "exceptions": [
    // ── The declared quality carve-out this story ratified ───────────────────────────────────────────
    {
      "model": "krea_2_turbo",
      "component": "controlBranch",
      "residentTier": "q8",
      "appliesToTiers": ["q4"],
      "cause": "packing-exception",
      "reason": "Packing the pose-control branch to q4 measures \"pose-locked; non-pose details drift\" — the control residual is precision-sensitive (RMS-clamped at τ) and is the thing the user actually asked for, so a q4 base floors its branch at q8 instead of following the tier down.",
      "evidence": {
        "state": "measured",
        "costGb": 1.8,
        "source": "config/manifests/builtin.models.jsonc `candle.control.branchPackSaveGb` (q8 −8.4, q4 −10.2 GB; the floor forgoes the 1.8 GB difference)",
        "note": "The q8 case is NOT an exception: on a q8 base the branch follows the tier exactly, which is why sc-15799 deleted the branch-quant lever outright rather than keeping its q8 rung."
      }
    },

    // ── Backend capability gap: MLX has no mxfp4 compute path (filed separately, sc-16014) ───────────
    {
      "model": "lens_turbo",
      "component": "textEncoder",
      "residentTier": "bf16",
      "appliesToTiers": ["q4", "q8"],
      "cause": "backend-capability",
      "reason": "The gpt-oss-20b MoE text encoder ships MXFP4 on disk and MLX has no mxfp4 compute path, so it is upcast to bf16 at load. No repackaging fixes this; it needs an mxfp4 compute path or a different published dtype.",
      "evidence": {
        "state": "measured",
        "costGb": 17.24,
        "source": "crates/sceneworks-worker/src/mlx_fit_gate.rs — the HEADROOM_GB calibration table (sc-10863): lens-turbo bf16 measures 28.43 GiB on disk / 45.67 GiB resident / 75.55 GiB peak; the 17.24 GiB in-memory weight expansion is resident − disk (1.61x).",
        "owedBy": "sc-16014",
        "note": "The bf16 tier is NOT above tier (bf16 is what the user selected), which is why appliesToTiers excludes it — but the 17.24 GiB was measured there, and it is the same upcast on every tier. The separate 29.88 GiB activation transient is not a residency exception and is out of scope for this ledger."
      }
    },
    {
      "model": "lens",
      "component": "textEncoder",
      "residentTier": "bf16",
      "appliesToTiers": ["q4", "q8"],
      "cause": "backend-capability",
      "reason": "Same gpt-oss MoE encoder and the same missing mxfp4 compute path as lens_turbo; the candle lane's bring-up path loads it MXFP4 → dense bf16 with quant = None.",
      "evidence": {
        "state": "unmeasured",
        "source": "crates/media/candle-gen/candle-gen-lens/src/text_encoder.rs — \"MXFP4 → dense bf16 (quant = None): the sc-5108 bring-up path (~40 GB resident)\"",
        "owedBy": "sc-16014",
        "note": "~40 GB is a whole-encoder resident figure, not the isolated upcast delta, so this row is unmeasured rather than borrowing lens_turbo's 17.24."
      }
    },

