    // ── Within-tier precision floors: a "q4" tier that is partly q8 ──────────────────────────────────
    // These are the sharpest cases in the ledger. The user selects q4 and gets q8 weights for part of
    // the model, decided inside the provider where neither the worker's tier resolver nor its quality
    // rank can see it. Declared here so the substitution is at least visible — but declaring is not
    // reconciling: SC-16025 owns the actual defect, which is that `effective_quant_label`, the asset
    // record and the evidence cell all still describe such a run as a plain "q4". Same class as the
    // sc-11042 NVFP4 and sc-12425 int8-convrot aliasing, and the cost here is already measured, so
    // SC-16025 is about the invisibility rather than the size.
    {
      "model": "mage_flow_base",
